API-10: recompute a conduit's slope when a node invert or link offset is set

swmm_node_set_invert_elev() and swmm_link_set_offset_up/_dn() are accepted
after swmm_engine_open() but only stored the value. The conduit slope is
computed during open by resolve_cross_references() and beta, q_full and
q_max from it, so the edit had no effect on swmm_link_get_slope() or on
kinematic-wave routing.

Add recompute_conduit_slope(ctx, j), which repeats the resolver's slope
steps for one conduit (without the warnings), reverses the conduit under
dynamic wave if it became adverse, as open does, and then calls
recompute_conduit_flow_properties(). The three setters call it in the
OPENED state for the affected conduits. Lengthening is applied later, in
Router::init, from the updated slope.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-10_swmm600.patch

